# stable-files - biobakery's core tables, as paths under results/: what a
# run's record keeps the checksums of, a re-run compares, and selftest checks.
# A line may add how the file is read for its checksum, as lib/outputs.sh says.
#
# Chosen by running its fixture jobs twice, then at another CPU count, as
# docs/migration.md's phase 6 notes record. Left out, because they vary from
# run to run with a known cause: Nonpareil's curves, since its k-mer mode
# subsamples at random with no seed; the BIOM files, which hold the time they
# were written; and the reports, PDFs and logs. Within tables: Nonpareil's
# columns of alpha_diversity.tsv. HUMAnN's tables are read with their numbers
# at 12 significant digits, since a sum's last digit varies from run to run.
kneaddata/read-counts.tsv
metaphlan/*.tsv
humann/*.tsv round 12
alpha_diversity.tsv drop nonpareil_diversity,coverage_pct,redundancy_pct,model_fit,effort_gbp,effort_95_gbp
motus/motus-counts.tsv
esviritu/virus-taxa.tsv
esviritu/virus-assemblies.tsv
esviritu/virus-contigs.tsv
esviritu/virus-coverage.tsv
esviritu/read-counts.tsv
markermagu/virome-counts.tsv
markermagu/virome-relab.tsv
markermagu/markermagu-profile.tsv
